+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01R5tED6H9QxHd8rTsKtzctv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three validation gates pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilt a permission-aware document management API with Express + TypeScript, in-memory storage.\n\n**Files created:**\n- `CONTRACT.md` — exhaustive behavior checklist (definition of done)\n- `src/store.ts` — domain types, in-memory `Store`, and permission resolution logic\n- `src/app.ts` — `createApp()` with all routes, auth middleware, sharing, cascade delete\n- `src/index.ts` — entry point (re-exports `createApp`, starts a server when run directly)\n- `src/app.test.ts` — 37 tests covering every contract criterion\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n\n- **Permission resolution** uses numeric role levels (viewer=1, editor=2, owner=3). `documentLevel()` takes the max of the document's owner status, direct document shares, *and* the inherited folder level — and `folderLevel()` recursively walks up the parent chain (cycle-guarded). This gives \"most permissive across all paths\" for free.\n- **Role gates:** read ≥ viewer, modify/share ≥ editor, delete/role-management = owner only. Granting the `owner` role or changing an *existing* share requires owner; creating a new viewer/editor share needs only editor.\n- **Cascade delete:** deleting a folder recursively removes child folders, contained documents, and all associated shares, logging each removal.\n- **Activity log** records create/update/delete/share with action, userId, targetType, targetId, and ISO timestamp.\n- **Hierarchy safety:** folder moves that would create a cycle (into self or a descendant) return 400.\n\n**Validation:**\n- `npm run build` → clean\n- `npm run lint` → clean\n- `npm test` → 37/37 passing\n\nThe tests were written per-criterion (register/login flows, auth rejection, CRUD, 400/403/404 boundaries, multi-path permission precedence, folder→document inheritance,